In 1991, Philip Zimmermann released PGP, bringing strong encryption to ordinary people.

The @NSAGov opposed its export, and the U.S. government investigated him for three years.

What was at stake? The right to use powerful cryptography without government permission.

That same cypherpunk spirit lives on in Ethereum Classic.

Proof-of-Work. Censorship resistance. Immutability.

Watch the full video from the Proof-of-Work Summit in Prague, co-hosted by @ETCCooperative.

https://youtu.be/bbdoUAu6jqU

